Package: pyport
Title: Convert 'Python' Packages into Native 'R' Packages
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("pyport authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "maintainer@example.com",
           comment = "PLACEHOLDER: replace with the real maintainer before release"),
    person("Max", "Brunsfeld", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of the vendored 'tree-sitter-python' grammar"),
    person("Tree-sitter authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "Tree-sitter C headers and parser.c")
  )
Description: Parses 'Python' source code without requiring a 'Python'
    installation and converts 'Python' packages into standalone 'R' packages
    that run natively in 'R'. Parsing uses a vendored 'tree-sitter' grammar
    for 'Python' together with the 'treesitter' package, and produces an
    abstract syntax tree that mirrors the 'Python' 'ast' module.
